    <!--
      172 — admin-ssh-issued-key : the issuance AUDIT record for admin SSH key-ISSUANCE
      (SSH PR-4, Option B; ships dark behind app.ssh-issue.enabled=false). One row per Ed25519
      keypair the BFF MINTS for an operator to SSH a licensed device. NON-SECRET only: the
      issued OpenSSH public line + its SHA256 fingerprint (the %f the node pins) + a FK to the
      backing device_ssh_license row whose key_fingerprints that fingerprint was added to. NO
      private-key column — the minted private key is held only in a short-TTL leader-pinned
      single-use in-memory store, streamed ONCE, never persisted. Revoke is a CAS
      issued->revoked (never deleted = audit) that ALSO removes the fingerprint from the backing
      license (bumping its generation to drive the export forward). Band 172 is the NEXT FREE
      band above the 170-171 ssh-terminal/image-build band; appended LAST after the 171 include.
      CLONES the 011/170 portable-DDL idioms verbatim (app-UUID PK, timestamptz now(), one
      changeSet per CHECK/FK/index/GRANT, PG-gated index+GRANT via dbms=postgresql
      onFail=MARK_RAN; NEVER a DELETE grant).
