    <!--
      301 — account.account_issuer: closes the multi-brand bff_-session domain-scope
      blocker. The introspect contract carried no brand/issuer field (only `provider`, the
      OAuth LOGIN provider — a different axis from the per-brand Casdoor instance), so
      user-bff's synthetic-Jwt filter could only stamp an `iss` via singleTrustedIssuerOrNull
      and stamped NOTHING on a genuinely multi-issuer cluster → PrincipalDomain.forScope
      resolved "__deny__" and EVERY domain-scoped bff_-session read/write failed closed.
      Persists the account's own Casdoor issuer at the ONE id_token decode point
      (InternalAccountController#ensureAccount, provider="casdoor") and surfaces it as the
      nullable `issuer` introspect field. SECURITY: the id_token is decoded but NOT
      signature-verified and the handle is user-bff-supplied, so — unlike 292's casdoor_sub
      (only ever ADDED to a deny-wins pin set) — the iss DECIDES TENANT SCOPE and is stamped
      ONLY on strict membership of the configured, NON-EMPTY commons-DomainRegistry
      trusted-issuer set; anything else stamps NULL and degrades to today's fail-closed deny.
      Nullable (legacy rows self-heal on next native login), NOT unique (a brand's accounts
      all share its issuer). Band 301: next free above 300. Appended LAST.
    -->
    <include file="db/changelog/301-account-issuer.xml"/>

